  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM &#x2013; Multi Country Humanitarian Assistance &#x2013; CAP 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">More than four years after the official end of the Islamic State of Iraq and the Levant (ISIL) crisis in Iraq, which led to violent conflict and massive displacement of populations, there have been significant improvements, but the humanitarian context remains complex and fragile. The post-conflict period has seen the gradual return of over 4.96 million people to their areas of origin, but, according to IOM&apos;s Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) as of June 2022, 1.17 million persons remain displaced in camps and informal displacement sites, out-of-camp settlements and host communities and are now facing protracted displacement. Through this project, depending on needs and evolving context, IOM&apos;s interventions include but are not limited to: provision of cash and multi-purpose cash assistance, provision of emergency shelter in camp and out-of-camp settings; provision of camp coordination and camp management in formal camp and informal sites; provision of essential healthcare and support to health facilities in camps and in areas with high levels of displacement and/or returns; provision of mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS) assistance services in camps and out-of-camp locations (including MHPSS and Livelihoods programme); and provision of protection case management, protection mainstreaming and protection monitoring.</narrative>
  </description>
